    "knowledge_point": "Calculating a Joint Probability Containing Inequalities From a Table",
    "problem": "|  | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ | $Y=5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{2}{9}$ |\n| $X=4$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{2}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ |\n\nCompute $P(X=4\\,\\,\\text{or}\\,\\,Y>4)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above.",
    "worked_solution": "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=4\\,\\,\\text{or}\\,\\,Y>4) & =P((X,Y)\\in \\{(2,5),(4,1),(4,3),(4,5)\\}) \\\\  & =P((X,Y)=(2,5))+P((X,Y)=(4,1)) \\\\  & +P((X,Y)=(4,3))+P((X,Y)=(4,5)) \\\\  & =f(2,5)+f(4,1)+f(4,3)+f(4,5) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}+\\frac{1}{9}+\\frac{2}{9}+\\frac{1}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
